        ['q' => 'Does TWIA cover wind and hail damage in San Marcos?', 'a' => '<p>Generally no. Hays County is not part of the Texas Windstorm Insurance Association catastrophe area, which covers certain coastal counties. San Marcos properties typically get wind and hail coverage from their regular property insurer, or from the Texas FAIR Plan where applicable.</p>'],
        ['q' => 'What is a separate wind/hail deductible?', 'a' => '<p>Many Texas policies apply a different deductible to wind and hail losses, often a percentage of the dwelling (Coverage A) limit rather than a flat dollar amount. A 1% or 2% deductible on a higher-value home can be several thousand dollars. Check your declarations page before you file so you know what to expect.</p>'],
