        ['q' => 'How long does an insurer have to handle a claim in Texas?', 'a' => '<p>Under the Texas Prompt Payment of Claims statute (Insurance Code Chapter 542), an insurer generally has 15 days after notice of a claim to acknowledge it, start investigating, and request information. It then generally has 15 business days after receiving everything it asked for to accept or reject the claim, or up to 45 more days if it tells you it needs more time, and must pay within 5 business days after accepting. Deadlines can be extended after a declared weather catastrophe. See <a href="/services/delayed-insurance-claims/">delayed insurance claims</a>.</p>'],
